Project Testing Phase
LegalEase: AI-Powered Legal Document Generator

Project Testing Phase

1. Introduction

The Project Testing Phase is an important stage in the development of LegalEase: AI-Powered Legal Document Generator. The main purpose of testing is to verify that the application works correctly, produces properly structured document drafts, handles errors, and provides a smooth user experience.

Testing is performed after development to identify and fix problems before the final project demonstration and deployment.

> LegalEase generates AI-assisted drafts. Testing can verify software behavior and output quality, but it cannot guarantee that a generated document is legally suitable for every situation or jurisdiction.




---

2. Objectives of Testing

The main objectives are:

Verify that all features work correctly.

Check whether user input is handled properly.

Test AI document generation.

Check the quality and structure of generated drafts.

Verify document preview and editing.

Test PDF/DOCX/TXT generation.

Identify and fix errors.

Check application usability.

Test security-related functions.

Ensure the complete workflow works correctly.



---

3. Testing Strategy

The following testing methods can be used:

Unit Testing
     ↓
Integration Testing
     ↓
System Testing
     ↓
User Interface Testing
     ↓
AI Output Testing
     ↓
Security Testing
     ↓
User Acceptance Testing


---

4. Unit Testing

Unit testing checks individual components separately.

Components tested

Form validation

Document type selection

AI prompt generation

AI response processing

Document formatting

PDF generation

DOCX generation

Database functions


Example

If the user leaves a required field empty:

Input:
Tenant Name = Empty

Expected:
"Please enter the tenant name."

If the correct information is entered, the validation should allow the request to continue.


---

5. Functional Testing

Functional testing verifies whether each feature performs its intended function.

Feature	Expected Result

Home Page	Opens correctly
Document Selection	Shows available document types
Input Form	Accepts user information
Validation	Detects missing/invalid input
AI Generation	Produces a structured draft
Preview	Displays generated content
Edit	Allows modifications
Regenerate	Produces updated draft
Download	Creates the selected file
Error Handling	Displays useful error messages



---

6. Document Selection Testing

Different document types are tested to make sure the correct form is displayed.

Example

When the user selects:

Rental Agreement

The system should display fields such as:

Owner name

Tenant name

Property information

Rent

Duration

Start date


When the user selects another document type, the relevant fields should change accordingly.


---

7. Input Validation Testing

The input form is tested with different types of information.

Test cases

Test 1 – Valid Input

Name: Anu
Date: 10/10/2026
Purpose: Authorization

Expected Result:
The system accepts the information.

Test 2 – Missing Required Field

Name: [Empty]

Expected Result:
The system displays a validation message.

Test 3 – Invalid Information

The system should identify invalid formats where validation rules apply.


---

8. AI Generation Testing

AI generation is one of the most important testing areas.

The system is tested with:

Complete information

Incomplete information

Different document types

Short input

Detailed input

Unusual but valid input


Expected result

The AI should:

Generate a structured draft.

Use the information provided by the user.

Maintain relevant details.

Avoid unnecessarily inventing important facts.

Clearly identify missing information when appropriate.



---

9. AI Output Quality Testing

Generated documents are manually reviewed for:

Correct names

Correct dates

Correct amounts

Proper headings

Logical structure

Readability

Missing sections

Unwanted information

Contradictions


Because AI output can vary, important documents should be reviewed by the user and, where appropriate, a qualified legal professional.


---

10. Prompt Testing

Different prompts are tested to determine whether the AI produces consistent results.

Example

Basic Prompt:

> Generate a rental agreement.



Improved Structured Prompt:

> Create a rental agreement draft using only the information provided. Organize the document into appropriate sections and do not invent important missing facts.



The structured approach should generally produce a more controlled output.


---

11. Document Preview Testing

The preview page is tested to ensure:

Complete content is displayed.

Headings are readable.

Paragraphs are correctly formatted.

No content is unnecessarily cut off.

Editing works correctly.

Long documents can be viewed properly.



---

12. Editing Testing

The editing feature is tested by changing generated information.

Example

Original:

> Monthly Rent: ₹10,000



After editing:

> Monthly Rent: ₹12,000



Expected Result:
The updated information should appear in the final document.


---

13. Download Testing

The download feature is tested for supported formats.

PDF

Check:

File creation

Formatting

Text visibility

Page layout


DOCX

Check:

File opens correctly

Text is present

Headings and paragraphs are readable


TXT

Check:

Complete text is included

File opens without errors



---

14. Integration Testing

Integration testing checks whether different modules work together.

Example

User Interface
      ↓
Input Form
      ↓
Backend
      ↓
AI API
      ↓
Generated Draft
      ↓
Document Generator
      ↓
Download

